Keep a shared counts as an empty list of whole numbers.
Keep a shared fresh as an empty list of whole numbers.
Keep a shared downs as an empty list of whole numbers.
Keep a shared rights as an empty list of whole numbers.
Keep a shared size as 0.
Keep a shared steps as 0.
Place 1 into downs.
Place 1 into downs.
Place -1 into downs.
Place -1 into downs.
Place 2 into downs.
Place 2 into downs.
Place -2 into downs.
Place -2 into downs.
Place 2 into rights.
Place -2 into rights.
Place 2 into rights.
Place -2 into rights.
Place 1 into rights.
Place -1 into rights.
Place 1 into rights.
Place -1 into rights.
Set size to 3.
Set steps to 2.
For every spot from 0 to 8.
Place 0 into counts.
Place 0 into fresh.

Set item 0 of counts to 1.

To wipe from marker (a whole number).
For every spot from 0 to 8.
Set item spot of fresh to 0.

To adopt from marker (a whole number).
For every spot from 0 to 8.
Set item spot of counts to item spot of fresh.

To jump from cell (a whole number).
The currentrow is cell divided by size.
The currentcolumn is cell modulo size.
For every move from 0 to 7.
The nextrow is currentrow plus item move of downs.
The nextcolumn is currentcolumn plus item move of rights.
If nextrow is at least 0 and nextrow is less than size and nextcolumn is at least 0 and nextcolumn is less than size.
The dest is nextrow times size plus nextcolumn.
Set item dest of fresh to item dest of fresh plus item cell of counts.

To spread from cell (a whole number).
If cell is at least 9, adopt from 0, return.
If item cell of counts is more than 0, jump from cell.
Spread from cell plus 1.

To begin from marker (a whole number).
Wipe from 0.
Spread from 0.

For every step from 1 to steps.
Begin from 0.

The numerator is 0.
For every spot from 0 to 8.
Set numerator to numerator plus item spot of counts.

The denominator is 1.
For every step from 1 to steps.
Set denominator to denominator times 8.

The headpart is numerator divided by denominator.
The remainder is numerator modulo denominator.
The parts is an empty list of text.
The headword is format whole number headpart as text.
Place headword into parts.
Place "." into parts.
For every digit from 0 to 9.
Set remainder to remainder times 10.
The part is remainder divided by denominator.
The digword is format whole number part as text.
Place digword into parts.
Set remainder to remainder modulo denominator.

The answer is join parts with "".
Repeat while the last position of answer is more than 1.
The final is the last position of answer.
The lastpiece is character final of answer.
If lastpiece is "0", remove last character from answer.
If lastpiece is not "0", stop.

The final is the last position of answer.
The lastpiece is character final of answer.
If lastpiece is ".", remove last character from answer.
Show answer.
